            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "I don’t have live internet access, so I can’t verify breaking updates after my knowledge cutoff. As of the latest information I know:\n\n- NASA’s **Perseverance rover** was continuing its exploration of **Jezero Crater**, a former lake basin on Mars.\n- It had been studying ancient river-delta and channel deposits, including areas associated with **Neretva Vallis**, an ancient river channel.\n- The rover continued collecting and sealing rock-core samples intended for a future **Mars Sample Return** mission.\n- NASA was reassessing the Mars Sample Return architecture because of cost and schedule concerns, while keeping Perseverance’s cached samples scientifically important.\n- The companion helicopter **Ingenuity** ended its mission in early 2024 after 72 flights, but Perseverance itself remained operational.\n\nFor the true latest news, the best sources are:\n\n- NASA Perseverance mission page: https://mars.nasa.gov/mars2020/\n- NASA Mars news: https://www.nasa.gov/mars/\n- Perseverance rover account on NASA/JPL social channels.",
